<title>JAPAN: Moody's assigns AAa to TEPCO bonds.</title>
<headline>Moody's assigns AAa to TEPCO bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Thursday it had assigned an Aaa rating to Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc's (TEPCO) 150 billion yen worth of 2.8 percent domestic bonds due in 2006 and to its 50 billion yen worth of 3.45 percent domestic bonds due in 2016.</p>
<p>Moody's said the rating was based on TEPCO's importance to Japan's economy and the very favourable industry operating environment.</p>
</text>
